<p>The U.S. military said it struck a vessel in the eastern Pacific on May 5, killing three men it described as “narco-terrorists.” U.S. Southern Command said the vessel was operated by unidentified “Designated Terrorist Organizations,” was traveling on known drug-trafficking routes and was engaged in drug-trafficking operations; no U.S. personnel were hurt. The Pentagon said another U.S. strike on an alleged drug boat in the Caribbean a day earlier killed two people, bringing the two-day toll to five and the campaign’s death toll to 190. U.S. officials and critics dispute whether the targets are combatants in an armed conflict or criminal suspects, and whether the strikes are lawful.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NqDLthg3Gu2QyozWyIQUHhiMAxCXeZlWTqnYXR09MOLzCAePsdwSIY4rp9l7wZubpaAFeT6medKah7Ox5E95Z89OJMK8pwe35_E3ollI_UpfIoinGeYVSrsYkH2lDul78vverTFMJ3oHUVbskLbHiLi4JiUTr5YrBOFv5xWgcfWdsQ3WECD7bxWEgO8P' alt='Image from a U.S. military video released in connection with the eastern Pacific strike' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evidence dispute: The Guardian and Sveriges Radio reported that U.S. authorities have not publicly provided evidence proving the targeted boats were involved in drug trafficking.</li><li>Operating waters: Noticias SIN reported that the Pacific attack occurred in international waters and described the broader campaign as taking place in international waters near Venezuela and Colombia.</li><li>Public footage: A video distributed by the U.S. military showed an explosion during a strike on what it described as an alleged drug vessel.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Southern Command: The command emphasized the operation’s chain of command, saying Joint Task Force Southern Spear acted under orders from SOUTHCOM commander Gen. Francis L. Donovan. (<a href='https://www.infobae.com/america/america-latina/2026/05/06/estados-unidos-ataco-una-nueva-narcolancha-en-el-pacifico-oriental-tres-muertos/'>Infobae</a>, <a href='https://www.milliyet.com.tr/dunya/son-dakika-abd-pasifikte-bir-tekneyi-daha-vurdu-can-kayiplari-var-7583070'>Milliyet</a>)</li><li>President Trump: President Trump has defended the maritime strikes, saying the United States is in armed conflict with Latin American cartels and needs to escalate action against drugs entering the country. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-military-strike-on-alleged-drug-boat-kills-three-in-the-eastern-pacific/article70945474.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Rights groups: Rights groups have described the sea strikes as extrajudicial killings, disputing Washington’s framing of the targets as combatants in a drug-related conflict. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/05/us-military-vessel-strike'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/3-killed-us-strike-suspected-drug-boat-eastern-pacific/'>3 killed in U.S. strike on suspected drug boat in eastern Pacific, Pentagon says</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/5-dead-in-us-strikes-on-alleged-drug-boats-off-latin-america-pentagon'>5 dead in US strikes on alleged drug boats off Latin America: Pentagon</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-military-strike-on-alleged-drug-boat-kills-three-in-the-eastern-pacific/article70945474.ece'>U.S. Military strike on alleged drug boat kills three in the eastern Pacific</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-us-military-boat-pacific-trump/'>U.S. military strikes vessel in Eastern Pacific, killing three</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/05/us-military-vessel-strike'>US military kills three people in boat strike in eastern Pacific</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.newsday.com/news/nation/trump-cartels-eastern-pacific-narco-drugs-t51552'>US military strike on alleged drug boat kill